    "updated_at": "2022-11-10T01:47:02Z",
    "body": "Most media controls I encounter on the web are provided by the sites themselves, and in my experience, I have _never_ seen the displayed duration change when the playbackRate changes. Changing the way duration and current time are displayed to the user is currently and trivially implementable through script. So I suspect there's not a huge demand for an easier way to do something that's easy to do already.\r\n\r\nAlso, with my browser implementer hat on, I don't agree that scaling the displayed timeline as a function of the playback rate is a good idea. For one, it makes certain user tasks much more difficult, such as \"go watch this video; the good part starts 3 minutes in\".",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
