    "created_at": "2022-11-10T02:36:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-11-10T02:37:01Z",
    "body": "I do see this implemented in mpv.io. There, if you set a specific playback rate, the remaining time is show per the playback rate. However, current time and duration are still the absolute times. A bit of both worlds, where a user can more easily know how much \"wall clock\" time is left, while being able to seek to \"the good part at 3 minutes\".\r\n\r\nI have also previously implemented a Video.js plugin that did this (https://github.com/videojs/videojs-playbackrate-adjuster) though, that plugin does adjust all times depending on the playback rate.\r\n\r\nMaybe if `video.remainingTime` was exposed, that could reflect the playback rate, otherwise, it seems to be too complicated and potentially a breaking change for folks who have UIs that adjust times based on the playback rate, wouldn't want to double apply that adjustment.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
